{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs","id":846038,"title":"Collected Secrets of the Covenants Open Development Blogs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T05:54:00-08:00","id":846038,"title":"Collected Secrets of the Covenants Open Development Blogs","content":"I noticed that sometimes I have trouble finding some of these links. I thought that maybe I'm not the only one.<br /> So I have collected them here for easy search.<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merits-and-rituals-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merit...n-development/</a><br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries-the-rites-of-the-dragon-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-m...e-the-requiem/</a><br /> <br /> Invictus: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/secrets-covenants-invictus/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/secrets-covenants-invictus/</a><br /> <br /> Lancea et Sanctum: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles-playtest-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-san...e-the-requiem/</a><br /> <br /> Carthian Movement: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/carthian-merits-and-law-the-voice-of-the-people/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/carthian-meri...of-the-people/</a><br /> <br /> I apologize if that's not allowed and ask to the mods to delete this post in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T10:42:53-07:00","id":851222,"title":"","content":"It said that next week all the art should be in, ... will that be the end and get us a PDF which we all YEARN for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:01:50-07:00","id":851231,"title":"","content":"After that there's probably a lot more layout, then turning it over to the developer to check, then back to layout, then to Paradox for approvals, then I believe is when the pdf becomes available.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong on a couple steps here but Rich has really explained it all in the Monday Meeting blog posts <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/heres-the-windup-and-the-pitch-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">like this one.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:14:40-07:00","id":851237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=851222#post851222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It said that next week all the art should be in, ... will that be the end and get us a PDF which we all YEARN for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That just means the art itself is in... it then has to go for approval as well as the book will move into the layout queue. Still at least a few months away from PDF release...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6991-mirthful_mike","name":"mirthful_mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T08:09:42-07:00","id":859654,"title":"","content":"This thread should be stickied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T11:49:41-07:00","id":892668,"title":"","content":"How much longer, external factors are finally resolved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T23:05:19-07:00","id":893057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=892668#post892668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much longer, external factors are finally resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't really know, maybe a few weeks or a month or two if I were to give it a guess, but so far as my estimates go it could be out tomorrow for all I know. Onyx Path doesn't really give time estimates for anything unless that estimate is &quot;it should be out next week.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T07:58:52-07:00","id":997694,"title":"","content":"This should be stickied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:19:08-07:00","id":997756,"title":"","content":"It definitely should be stickied.<br /> <br /> Jesus christ the oaths are powerful as all fuck. Some of them would definitely benefit from clarification, though. Like, do the effect of the oath of the true knight apply to all vampires or just Invictus vampires ? Can you seriously just take an oath and have free supernatural armor forever (not to mention the immunity to ingesting vampire blood) ? What the heck ? And the Oath of abstinence, pay vitae and willpower, never have to spend vitae to wake up. Seriously, how many years has the Ordo Dracul put into doing that kind of stuff ?<br /> <br /> I'm really split about these. On the one hand, I love how they expand upon Invictus mentality and trivia (knights, prisoner etiquette...), but on the other hand, as has been pointed out countless times I'm sure, what the heck is up with these powers, where do they come from, who invented them, how do they exist ? How do the Circle of the Crone have to do elaborate rituals that can take hours for effects that vary from awesome to not too bad while all the Invictus has to do is sign a paper ? Same thing with the Carthian law of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T10:57:51-07:00","id":997776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It definitely should be stickied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can do.<br /> <br /> [EDIT]Ok, apparently can't do on mobile. Will do when I get home from work.[/EDIT]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jesus christ the oaths are powerful as all fuck. Some of them would definitely benefit from clarification, though. Like, do the effect of the oath of the true knight apply to all vampires or just Invictus vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Oaths can be sworn <i>by</i> vampires of any Covenant as long as they meet the prerequisites (which sometimes includes Invictus Status), but can only be sworn <i>to</i> Invictus. So, that part kind of only applies to other Invictus. As for the Vinculum part, I would imagine it applies to all vampires. Even if it didn't, I can't imagine an Invictus Notary agreeing to preside over an Oath of True Knoghthood sworn by someone who was blood bound to a non-Invictus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you seriously just take an oath and have free supernatural armor forever (not to mention the immunity to ingesting vampire blood) ? What the heck ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;immunity&quot; to ingesting vampire blood is a drawback. You can't willingly drink it, which makes life pretty hard if your Blood Potency is 6 or higher, and if someone forces or tricks you into drinking it unknowingly or unwillingly, you take aggravated damage and are still at risk of being blood bound. Which would probably end the Oath, since not being blood bound is one of the conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Oath of abstinence, pay vitae and willpower, never have to spend vitae to wake up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until the next time you feed, at which point the Oath ends and you get 5 Merit dots to spend with Sanctity Merits. Theoretically you might never need to feed again since you don't have to spend Vitae to wake up, but you <i>do</i> need to spend Vitae to fuel any of your abilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how many years has the Ordo Dracul put into doing that kind of stuff ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ordo probably wouldn't consider the Oath of Abstinence worthwhile because it just trades one weakness for another. They don't want to have to sacrifice their Disciplines to escape the cycle of feeding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really split about these. On the one hand, I love how they expand upon Invictus mentality and trivia (knights, prisoner etiquette...), but on the other hand, as has been pointed out countless times I'm sure, what the heck is up with these powers, where do they come from, who invented them, how do they exist ? How do the Circle of the Crone have to do elaborate rituals that can take hours for effects that vary from awesome to not too bad while all the Invictus has to do is sign a paper ? Same thing with the Carthian law of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote David Hill, the answer to that question is a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-03-2016, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:21:49-07:00","id":997818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997776#post997776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Oaths can be sworn <i>by</i> vampires of any Covenant as long as they meet the prerequisites (which sometimes includes Invictus Status), but can only be sworn <i>to</i> Invictus. So, that part kind of only applies to other Invictus. As for the Vinculum part, I would imagine it applies to all vampires. Even if it didn't, I can't imagine an Invictus Notary agreeing to preside over an Oath of True Knoghthood sworn by someone who was blood bound to a non-Invictus.<br /> <br /> The &quot;immunity&quot; to ingesting vampire blood is a drawback. You can't willingly drink it, which makes life pretty hard if your Blood Potency is 6 or higher, and if someone forces or tricks you into drinking it unknowingly or unwillingly, you take aggravated damage and are still at risk of being blood bound. Which would probably end the Oath, since not being blood bound is one of the conditions.<br /> <br /> The Ordo probably wouldn't consider the Oath of Abstinence worthwhile because it just trades one weakness for another. They don't want to have to sacrifice their Disciplines to escape the cycle of feeding.<br /> <br /> <br /> To quote David Hill, the answer to that question is a chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a weird answer, then. It's such a basic thing now, that this is unsatisfying. Did the Carthian movement randomly discover they could do weird shit by voting ? Ho do the Circle, Lance and Ordo feel about secular groups getting powers out of seemingly nowhere ? This makes those things way more mysterious than Theban Sorcery, Cruac and Mysteries which is weird as hell. At least, those have some lore associated to them, divine powers bestowed upon the sanctified, the mystical power contained within blood that may or may not have been taught by the strix, the careful study of vampire biology and curse to find the loopholes and exploit them. Those already already full of secrets and questions. Meanwhile, the Invictus signs a paper and it does shit because of course. Wat.<br /> <br /> But whatever, more importantly :<br /> <br /> I don't read the oath the same way you do, which is part of what I'm saying when I find them unclear : &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If another coerces, tricks, or forces her to take his blood, he suffers a level of aggravated damage.</span></span>&quot;The way I understand it, it's the vampire who tricks the knight into drinking their blood who takes damage. Also, to me, the fact the blood &quot;turns to ash in her mouth&quot; would prevent the vinculum.<br /> <br /> I guess the not being able to drink vampire blood is a problel if you're BP 6+, but the way I understand it, this is the point where most other vampires start looking at you funny, expecting you to do the reasonable thing and just go sleep it off for a century.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, the Ordo Dracul wouldn't like the limitations of the oath of abstinence, but it's a hell of a starting point for a coil. Understanding how that works would help a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:55:10-07:00","id":997841,"title":"","content":"Theban rituals were found in a hidden chamber in Thebes. Longinus claims to be directed there by an angel, so they say God put them there. There's really no concrete explanation for them beyond 'God did it,' and the Lance stifles investigations into it. Cruac doesn't seem to have much explanation, either. They've just been around longer.<br /> <br /> Based on what we know about existing vampire magics, I believe that they're all just extensions of a vampire's Predatory Aura. An Oath hardens one vampire's Aura into another, the Carthians can 'amass' their Aura together so that it can affect an entire territory.<br /> <br /> That said, these examples are just the first draft versions of the powers, and they've been presented to the community and talked about for about two years. It's probably safe to say things have changed regarding clarity and power. In addition they are small parts of a larger book, which may go farther into explaining these powers, or at least in-character theories that are as verifiable as those regarding Cruac and Theban sorceries or the Coils and Scales of the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:10:47-07:00","id":997846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997818#post997818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a weird answer, then. It's such a basic thing now, that this is unsatisfying. Did the Carthian movement randomly discover they could do weird shit by voting ? Ho do the Circle, Lance and Ordo feel about secular groups getting powers out of seemingly nowhere ? This makes those things way more mysterious than Theban Sorcery, Cruac and Mysteries which is weird as hell. At least, those have some lore associated to them, divine powers bestowed upon the sanctified, the mystical power contained within blood that may or may not have been taught by the strix, the careful study of vampire biology and curse to find the loopholes and exploit them. Those already already full of secrets and questions. Meanwhile, the Invictus signs a paper and it does shit because of course. Wat.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the more mystically inclined Covenants would have a greater interest in and better means of investigating the source of their various magics. I would imagine they would be curious how Blood Oaths and Carthian law work, but I don't imagine the Invictus or the Carthians are too keen on letting the folks with more magical knowledge investigating too closely how their advantage works.<br /> <br /> If I were to make a guess, I would hypothesize that Carthian Law and Blood Oaths are tapping into the same source, some inherent property of the Blood that gives it power over the metaphysical concept of law.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind everything we know about Oaths and Law so far comes from 1e when they were pretty minor elements, and the 2e core. It's entirely possible Secrets of the Covenants might contain more details about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But whatever, more importantly :<br /> <br /> I don't read the oath the same way you do, which is part of what I'm saying when I find them unclear : &amp;quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If another coerces, tricks, or forces her to take his blood, he suffers a level of aggravated damage.</span></span>&amp;quot;The way I understand it, it's the vampire who tricks the knight into drinking their blood who takes damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you're correct about that. I misread the pronoun on who was taking the damage. I'm... Not convinced that isn't a typo, but from the information presented, yes, that's how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, to me, the fact the blood &amp;quot;turns to ash in her mouth&amp;quot; would prevent the vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The full sentence is <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;If she attempts to ingest Kindred Vitae, the blood turns to ash in her mouth.&quot;</span></span>. &quot;If she attempts&quot; sounds to me like something that requires her intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the not being able to drink vampire blood is a problel if you're BP 6+, but the way I understand it, this is the point where most other vampires start looking at you funny, expecting you to do the reasonable thing and just go sleep it off for a century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That's not an assumption I play under, but alright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997756#post997756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, yeah, the Ordo Dracul wouldn't like the limitations of the oath of abstinence, but it's a hell of a starting point for a coil. Understanding how that works would help a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure would. That's one of the best reasons for the Invictus to not want any Dragons studying their Oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:30:43-07:00","id":997859,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think other vampires are like &quot;Time for you to go into torpor.&quot; I think vampires go into torpor at BP 6+ largely because it is difficult for them to get vitae. So a Kindred who has little difficulty with that has little reason to voluntarily go into torpor. Plus, there are several ways around the feeding restriction (based on Covenant)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:31:15-07:00","id":997860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997846#post997846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. That's not an assumption I play under, but alright.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure would. That's one of the best reasons for the Invictus to not want any Dragons studying their Oaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>That probably depends on the domains and covenants. The Circle of the Crone have two whole mythological roles for those people and they would probably be some of the more accepting vampires when it comes to that. On the other hand, I seem to remember that in the 1E core book Augusto Vidal was said to be preparing for torpor as his BP meant human blood started not being enough for him. In the supplement about New Orleans, I think he had an overcomplicated plot about blood bonding a whole coterie so he'd have a perfectly loyal group of vampires he'd be able to feed from without being ratted out, this is definitely a thing on occasions.<br /> <br /> About the Ordo studying the oaths, since oaths can be signed with outsiders, it sounds pretty easy for a dragon to sign one and also go to his chapterhouse to show what they can do now. And yeah, the Invictus isn't as mystically oriented as the Lancea and Circle, but the oaths, as they are, are a huge source of power, you'd think the prospect of more power would make them look further. They've been here for what 1500 years a least. The Cruac's lore is less vague than that, and it's from a super recent covenant that aggregated lots of completely different weird cults and faiths.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the Oaths and Law in general, it's a matter of personal preference I guess. I can't understand the decision to give the Invictus and Carthians mystical powers when nothing really justifies that, except maybe making sure players who choose those covenants don't feel left out because they don't have magic. That the Invictus would have access to artifacts they have amassed like the Aegis Kai Doru because they're rich and powerful, I would accept no problem. For the Carthians, I don't know, but it feels weird that they have magic anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:43:42-07:00","id":997867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997860#post997860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Ordo studying the oaths, since oaths can be signed with outsiders, it sounds pretty easy for a dragon to sign one and also go to his chapterhouse to show what they can do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the Oath of the True Knight, since it requires Invictus Status 2. Unless they were dual-Covenant, but secret sharing is a <i>big</i> no-no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997860#post997860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, the Invictus isn't as mystically oriented as the Lancea and Circle, but the oaths, as they are, are a huge source of power, you'd think the prospect of more power would make them look further. They've been here for what 1500 years a least. The Cruac's lore is less vague than that, and it's from a super recent covenant that aggregated lots of completely different weird cults and faiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure they look into creating new Oaths, but they're probably not super concerned with, nor well equipped for figuring out where they come from. Who knows maybe there's some methuselah somewhere bound by the first Blood Oath to some demonic entity of unspeakable power, and the terms of that contract allow other Invictus to make limited use of the demonic entity's contract negotiation powers. Wouldn't discovering that make a cool chronicle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997860#post997860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Oaths and Law in general, it's a matter of personal preference I guess. I can't understand the decision to give the Invictus and Carthians mystical powers when nothing really justifies that, except maybe making sure players who choose those covenants don't feel left out because they don't have magic. That the Invictus would have access to artifacts they have amassed like the Aegis Kai Doru because they're rich and powerful, I would accept no problem. For the Carthians, I don't know, but it feels weird that they have magic anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not the first person to express distaste for the secular Covenants having access to something resembling blood magic. I recall quite a stink being made about it on the old forums when the Blood Oaths and Carthian Law Merits in the core book were first spoiled. If you don't like them, you don't have to use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:06:03-07:00","id":997877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997841#post997841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what we know about existing vampire magics, I believe that they're all just extensions of a vampire's Predatory Aura. An Oath hardens one vampire's Aura into another, the Carthians can 'amass' their Aura together so that it can affect an entire territory.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a <i>really </i>cool explanation... I never would've thought of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:07:07-07:00","id":997878,"title":"","content":"I find the Carthian and Invictus merits to add a lot to the game. I mean it's not clear how they got these abilities, but hopefully there'll be some elucidation in Secrets of the Covenants. Overall, I prefer to have blood oaths and Carthian law over not having them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:11:12-07:00","id":997880,"title":"","content":"I always felt they were related to blood sympathy somehow. As in by having the majority of kindred in a given area believe strongly in something (a law) you enact or transfer it to all kindreds in the area through blood sympathy. (There are many holes in that theory tho :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:59:31-07:00","id":997934,"title":"","content":"No, not the knight oath, but any oath is a starting point for a dedicated dragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997867#post997867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure they look into creating new Oaths, but they're probably not super concerned with, nor well equipped for figuring out where they come from. Who knows maybe there's some methuselah somewhere bound by the first Blood Oath to some demonic entity of unspeakable power, and the terms of that contract allow other Invictus to make limited use of the demonic entity's contract negotiation powers. Wouldn't discovering that make a cool chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be I guess, but then I hope mysteries of the covenants expands on that.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I do remember being baffled back when I read Blood and Smoke and seeing lots of posts on forums (might have been this one or others) that were mostly wondering why that was something that needed to exist in the first place. Maybe some people warmed up to it, maybe some saw it wasn't going away and just got used to it. I still see it as an attempt to fix something that wasn't broken, thematically absurd for those covenants and no, I'm not using it, and would think twice about playing in a campaign where that was a thing (except maybe a one shot). I mean, there are few things I'm cold towards in 2E like the social maneuvering, the conditions that I find a bit clunky to use, but I think I see the point and I can work around them if I want. The two new magicks is just something I look at and think &quot;Why would you do that ?&quot; every time I see them, and the only sane reaction seems to take a giant hacksaw to that whole section.<br /> <br /> Well, almost. Again, I really like the flavor the oaths give. If anything, I'd use that as Invictus fluff because that tells me so much about the covenant's potential mentality, habits, customs, etc. I wouldn't have the knight oath, but have an official position recognized by most Invictus governments with matching expectations and privileges for example. In general, I'm really impressed by how all of those new sections are written (independently of whether I agree with the powers or not). They're all much more appealing and exciting than they were before and there's really kind of a theme going on while in the core book, they sorta felt like a series of random powers.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Invictus, I'm also honestly kind of surprised at how that almost makes them look like kinda not so bad people. The model prisoner oath for instance, or the knight oath. For a group that's often been written as super corrupt and oppressive, it's pretty nice of them to value treating people well and to value neutrality like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:36:37-07:00","id":997977,"title":"","content":"The oaths and laws add a lot of good flavor to the Invictus and the Carthians. I fully intend on using them in my upcoming chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:28:36-07:00","id":998002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997860#post997860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That probably depends on the domains and covenants. The Circle of the Crone have two whole mythological roles for those people and they would probably be some of the more accepting vampires when it comes to that. On the other hand, I seem to remember that in the 1E core book Augusto Vidal was said to be preparing for torpor as his BP meant human blood started not being enough for him. In the supplement about New Orleans, I think he had an overcomplicated plot about blood bonding a whole coterie so he'd have a perfectly loyal group of vampires he'd be able to feed from without being ratted out, this is definitely a thing on occasions.<br /> <br /> About the Ordo studying the oaths, since oaths can be signed with outsiders, it sounds pretty easy for a dragon to sign one and also go to his chapterhouse to show what they can do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends really. What do they have to show exactly? Some oaths need a notary to administer. A notary is status 3 minimum and an established reputation for maintaining the status quo and Invictus superiority. So if you have the domain's only notary with a personal dislike of the Ordo Dracul or some other status 3+ Invictus decides to restrict or forbid Ordo members from being eligible for oaths then they don't have anything. Nor do you know the costs and benefits associated with the liege. Furthermore it's ridiculously simple to stipulate that discussing the terms or specifics of an oath or attempting to dissect the powers behind them constitutes a violation of the oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:30:26-07:00","id":998017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997934#post997934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, I do remember being baffled back when I read Blood and Smoke and seeing lots of posts on forums (might have been this one or others) that were mostly wondering why that was something that needed to exist in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I recall on the old forums, it was just one dude who was super not into blood magic of any kind upset that the two Covenants he liked were getting blood magic. He mostly settled down after a few non-Oath, non-Law Carthian and Invictus Merits were spoiled, but it was one of those subjects he'd pop in to reassure everyone that he didn't like blood magic and thought there should be Covenants without access to it any time it came up. Most other folks were just like &quot;Ok. I think it's cool. You can always just ban them in your games if you don't like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=997934#post997934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some people warmed up to it, maybe some saw it wasn't going away and just got used to it. I still see it as an attempt to fix something that wasn't broken, thematically absurd for those covenants and no, I'm not using it, and would think twice about playing in a campaign where that was a thing (except maybe a one shot).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Sorry you feel that way, I think they're awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T19:43:45-07:00","id":998025,"title":"","content":"Invictus Oaths and Carthian Law are not new concepts, they were both introduced in their respective covenant books ten years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T20:29:15-07:00","id":998048,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I really like the Invictus Oaths and Carthian Laws. I feel like it adds a bit of mystery to a chronicle, and it reminds the more mystically inclined covenants (the Ordo, the Circle, and the Sanctum) that the Invictus and the Carthians have a few tricks up their sleeves. (Also, an Invictus Knight with Reslience sounds just as scary as a Red Dragon, in my opinion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:21:23-07:00","id":998536,"title":"","content":"Count me in those that think the Oaths and Law are awesome.<br /> <br /> They make as much sense as vampires do, so I don't see the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T02:37:43-08:00","id":1002805,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I needed a collection like this. Perfect material for my long-seated personal project of translating VtM to VtR under my own terms. I'm planning to have the Bloodline Gifts be either a set of Devotions, a set of free Merits, or a set of advanced Merits.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there's the Translation Guide out, and other people have their own homebrews, but I'm a wannabe Mage with a not-so wannabe Obsession <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T14:09:45-08:00","id":1003593,"title":"","content":"it looks like we may be a month or so from FINALLY being finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:28:57-08:00","id":1003698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1003593#post1003593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it looks like we may be a month or so from FINALLY being finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope so. Hard to support a product line when there is no product line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:04:44-08:00","id":1003716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1003593#post1003593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it looks like we may be a month or so from FINALLY being finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have citation for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:20:40-08:00","id":1003723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1003716#post1003716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have citation for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in proofing. That doesn't necessarily mean it'll be done in &quot;a month or so&quot;, but it is the last step in the process, so it'll probably be done soon. This is usually the point in the process I allow myself to start getting hyped. But, you know, Mage was in proofing for a long time, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-15-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T03:22:18-08:00","id":1003841,"title":"","content":"Proofing? Why would the maker of the book need a month to determine whether the book exists or not? What is this, Schrodinger: the Breathing?<br /> <br /> (I tease. Thank you for explaining it. A pre december release would be fantastic for gift buying purposes.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T08:26:09-08:00","id":1003953,"title":"","content":"Have you even looked at how hard it is to empirically prove that something is real? Your hallucinated reality is already hella different from my own, and then we're forced to use symbolic language to communicate!<br /> <br /> I mean, geez, Mage ever even coming OUT of proofing is evidence someone hit it with heavy prime to imbue sufficient Truth. <br /> <br /> Or a Working of Imperium occurred. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Books by the holidays would be nice, yes, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T13:09:43-08:00","id":1004077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1003716#post1003716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have citation for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>monday meeting notes say &quot;Proofing&quot; <br /> <br /> this usualy means that the end is very night, and some earliy drafts wind up on DTRPG early to let us help with errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-16-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:36:15-08:00","id":1004225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004077#post1004077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">monday meeting notes say &amp;quot;Proofing&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> this usualy means that the end is very night, and some earliy drafts wind up on DTRPG early to let us help with errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been in proofing for about 2 months with no word on it from Rich","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:51:40-08:00","id":1004229,"title":"","content":"Yeah this proofing has taken a lot longer, as far as I can tell, than most others.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining it's because of the setup, which isn't your traditional two columns of text book.<br /> <br /> And I believe Rich has spoken about it repeatedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:17:15-08:00","id":1004236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004229#post1004229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah this proofing has taken a lot longer, as far as I can tell, than most others.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining it's because of the setup, which isn't your traditional two columns of text book.<br /> <br /> And I believe Rich has spoken about it repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>He gave excuses and promises that they would be working to speed up the process. He hasn't said, there are complications in proofing due to X, we estimate it will be finished by Christmas. <br /> <br /> There is zero point in radio silence of this project at this phase. During development phase yeah I can see keeping a little quiet, no clue what they will be able to fit in the book.<br /> <br /> Last time rich said anything about it that I saw was when it just hit layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:20:21-08:00","id":1004237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004236#post1004236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He gave excuses and promises that they would be working to speed up the process. He hasn't said, there are complications in proofing due to X, we estimate it will be finished by Christmas.<br /> <br /> There is zero point in radio silence of this project at this phase. During development phase yeah I can see keeping a little quiet, no clue what they will be able to fit in the book.<br /> <br /> Last time rich said anything about it that I saw was when it just hit layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>November 8th, '<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Secrets of the Covenants is being handled as it needs to be. You are going to be amazed at the design of this book, but that takes time.'</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Really these things aren't excuses, they're just telling it like it is. Some books take a long time for proofing, apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:29:16-08:00","id":1004241,"title":"","content":"Meh that tells us exactly nothing.<br /> <br /> Hey guys we are still working on project x. See you next Monday. <br /> <br /> I mean actual details. We are through proofing chapter 3 of 6 (or whatever it is.)<br /> That is information. We have at least some idea each time we see one of those.<br /> <br /> That builds anxiety and hype. The former builds frustration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","user":"overload","date":". 11-17-2016, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:32:17-08:00","id":1004242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004241#post1004241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh that tells us exactly nothing.<br /> <br /> Hey guys we are still working on project x. See you next Monday.<br /> <br /> I mean actual details. We are through proofing chapter 3 of 6 (or whatever it is.)<br /> That is information. We have at least some idea each time we see one of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that it would matter what section of the book we can't see is taking longer. And I'd imagine it's something more about the layout than any specific text.<br /> <br /> Have you tried asking? Rich Thomas responds to most questions I've seen posted by commenters in the Monday Meeting blogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T21:34:29-08:00","id":1004243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004242#post1004242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you tried asking? Rich Thomas responds to most questions I've seen posted by commenters in the Monday Meeting blogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen lots of people ask about a time line for various products and he gives nothing of substance. I'll go post a question though and we will see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T23:32:56-08:00","id":1004272,"title":"","content":"I just need the mechanics.... they can send it afterwards in its full form.<br /> <br /> Also there is not that much in official books for second edition of Requiem is this a trend or they plan to support it more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:25:25-08:00","id":1004346,"title":"","content":"Im hoping the end is in sight. all we can do is hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T09:53:06-08:00","id":1004487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004272#post1004272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just need the mechanics.... they can send it afterwards in its full form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be willing to bet, though only a small amount, that the mechanics we've been given in open development is all the mechanics available. They've likely been altered, since they were first drafts, but the entire book is in clanbook format and that left very little at the end for mechanics. Most of them were fluff.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's probably some accompanying explanation for how things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also there is not that much in official books for second edition of Requiem is this a trend or they plan to support it more? </div> </div> </div>Rich said not every book will get things every year. There's already two or three more books planned for vampire, however. I'd expect that as need for supplements dies down with Beast, Demon and Mummy, things will speed up for everyone else. Also if White Wolf decides to ever publish things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T15:48:49-08:00","id":1004679,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s where it is in the progress list:<br /> Proofing<br /> \u2022Secrets of the Covenants<br /> Please see my response to Victor earlier in the comments for a longer commentary on why that is all the info available. Short version, the info on the list is as transparent as our crew is comfortable being, and we\u2019re gonna stick with that for now. Thanks!<br /> <br /> So here ya go nofather. This is RichT's response.<br /> Like I said, excuses.<br /> <br /> I read his response to Victor which equated to this, just longer winded. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure why they have such little faith in their product, I've been more than satisfied with everything 2e I've purchased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:23:20-08:00","id":1004696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004679#post1004679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read his response to Victor which equated to this, just longer winded.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why they have such little faith in their product, I've been more than satisfied with everything 2e I've purchased.</div> </div> </div> </div>He said that the last time Mike explained what was going on people harassed him. So presumably they're not talking about whatever the hold up is because of harassment.<br /> <br /> It's not being held up for no reason, it will be out when it's out and no complaining will make that come faster.<br /> <br /> If you want some sort of insider track, you're free to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">apply for a job</a> with Onyx Path so you can be 'in' on the details you want to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:34:36-08:00","id":1004700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1004696#post1004696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He said that the last time Mike explained what was going on people harassed him. So presumably they're not talking about whatever the hold up is because of harassment.<br /> <br /> It's not being held up for no reason, it will be out when it's out and no complaining will make that come faster.<br /> <br /> If you want some sort of insider track, you're free to <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/&amp;quot;]apply</a> for a job[/URL] with Onyx Path so you can be 'in' on the details you want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in my response to rich, they are content producers. Criticism comes with the territory as well as trolls.<br /> <br /> Most content producers look for constructive criticism to make their products better, and the truly experienced can filter trolls with ease.<br /> <br /> I'm criticizing the process not the people. And while I want it out asap I'm not trying to rush them, just asking for some transparency. Maybe that's too much to ask.<br /> <br /> I would love to work for them. But I doubt they would pay as well as my current job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:18:17-08:00","id":1004778,"title":"","content":"Seeing how the sausage gets made doesn't always make the process less opaque.<br /> <br /> For the sake of explanation, let's use the proofing example. Basically, if you want chapter by chapter feedback on what's being proofed in a book, you're just not going to get it. It wouldn't actually be very useful information anyway. Putting a number on this kind of thing is inherently deceptive. Often, the proofreader has to go over a second proof (or a third!), making that number immediately invalid. Someone who doesn't understand how proofing works will--inevitably--make a comment about how <i>&quot;IT WAS AT CHAPTER 5 BUT NOW IT'S AT 2 WHAT GIVES YOU NEVER HIT DEADLINES!&quot; </i>and then Rich will have to patiently explain (like he always does) that it's more complicated than that and that it's not always a linear progression and that there's a limit to the expectations you can get out of these things and I'm already tired on his behalf just thinking about it.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to jump down your throat, but I do editing and proofing as part of my day job. Proofing is a long, boring, not-easily-digestible process. We don't expect our proofreader to make that kind of granular report; it'd be a waste of her time and ours. I can't speak for other publishers--including OPP--but putting that information out into the wild so easily backfires. For everyone who's satisfied with that info, there's another group that thinks it's not enough, or who misunderstand it. The detail Rich puts into Monday Meetings is actually pretty remarkable for a publisher, RPG or otherwise. Like, we're kind of at maximum transparency here, beyond getting into the nitty-gritty of the publishing process, and that requires time and effort from freelancers who usually have day jobs.<br /> <br /> In the case of <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>, specifically, it's a big book with a lot of moving parts: lots of artwork, in-character documents, special fonts, etc. (or that's the impression I've got from blog previews and what not). Have a look at any of the Clanbooks for Requiem, and you'll get an idea of what it'll look like. It's not something that can be done fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:50:11-08:00","id":1004788,"title":"","content":"Ah but you see you just gave me more insight into the process. I've been asking and nobody had explained. <br /> But just coming out and saying it's a big book with lots of fiddly bits, and that it takes multiple proofs sometimes. <br /> <br /> I don't take it as you jumping down my throat. <br /> <br /> However, even rich said we use to get some updates. A word every now and then, even an acknowledgement goes a long way. Looking every week to see the Monday Meeting with proofing SotC is depressing.<br /> <br /> Yeah the clan books for requiem were awesome and nowhere near as big as what I imagine SotC is going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T05:07:35-08:00","id":1004882,"title":"","content":"The fact that Rich keeps us up to date on where in the process pretty much all of OPP's books are is, or at least used to be, pretty unusual. The Monday Meeting Notes usually gives me more information than I really need. I totally understand wanting to know more, but OPP is being very transparent as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:20:53-08:00","id":1005010,"title":"","content":"Hmm well it's been a while since I have paid any real attention to the boards. Maybe I'm spoiled. I remember the days of Rose chatting in and giving her 2 cents etc. She always seemed happy and excited to give us little spoilers.<br /> <br /> Even think I talked to Mike a couple of times. <br /> <br /> Now they seem very reclusive. Guess I missed whatever fallout happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:29:42-08:00","id":1005016,"title":"","content":"Rose hasn't been as active recently, presumably because she's been incredibly busy, but she still pops in from time to time. Dave and David are both pretty active. Matt I think kind of withdrew after the post-release Promethean drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:20:43-08:00","id":1005177,"title":"","content":"Wasn't she, for a time, also recovering from some sort of health issue? I never could figure it out if it was an injury or health condition. But I seem to remember that being a thing. I might be mixing people and/or situations up though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:29:57-08:00","id":1005184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1005177#post1005177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't she, for a time, also recovering from some sort of health issue? I never could figure it out if it was an injury or health condition. But I seem to remember that being a thing. I might be mixing people and/or situations up though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember exactly. She had hurt her arm. Don't know if it was a rotator cuff injury or if it was broke. She came on and chatted with us about it when she was able.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T00:18:54-08:00","id":1005266,"title":"","content":"Also that the injury reduced Rose's output to like 10% of normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T18:51:50-08:00","id":1005535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1005016#post1005016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rose hasn't been as active recently, presumably because she's been incredibly busy, but she still pops in from time to time. Dave and David are both pretty active. Matt I think kind of withdrew after the post-release Promethean drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was the drama? I'm dreadfully out of the loop.<br /> <br /> (Also, I hope Rose becomes less busy/injured soon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:16:24-08:00","id":1005558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1005535#post1005535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was the drama? I'm dreadfully out of the loop.<br /> <br /> (Also, I hope Rose becomes less busy/injured soon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There was more shenanigans involving people disliking the buy-in and themes of Promethean, and in general making ideological or personal attacks on Matt and his work. Insisting the game was broken, or unfinished, or limited. It... wasn't pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:47:39-08:00","id":1005760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1005535#post1005535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was the drama? I'm dreadfully out of the loop.<br /> <br /> (Also, I hope Rose becomes less busy/injured soon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It was honestly quite horrifying. I mean, yeah there were some things I didn't like about the book at first, but that was mostly until I actually got into the book. I think it mostly stemmed from people reading part of the book, and then getting on the forums to complain about it; it then devolved into some really ugly stuff afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:42:59-08:00","id":1009604,"title":"","content":"So according to the Monday Meeting Notes, this book should be out on OBS in two weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T19:58:31-08:00","id":1009607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1009604#post1009604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So according to the Monday Meeting Notes, this book should be out on OBS in two weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, and so should Hurt Locker. I'm so excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T20:23:55-08:00","id":1009616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/846038-collected-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development-blogs?p=1005760#post1005760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was honestly quite horrifying. I mean, yeah there were some things I didn't like about the book at first, but that was mostly until I actually got into the book. I think it mostly stemmed from people reading part of the book, and then getting on the forums to complain about it; it then devolved into some really ugly stuff afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, it actually drove me off of the forums for a while too because it was so caustic. Hopefully Matt will make his way back once he's ready. His insights are always helpful. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, I'm so psyched for Secrets of the Covenants to finally be here. Two weeks from now will be a good time, and it will be fitting reward for having plowed through a major project at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD